      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHAMPAGNE BABY (8) is the top pick with a setup that can bring sharp improvement, even though her latest figures read modestly. She was last in a Goulburn Mdn over 1600m but was beaten just over five lengths after covering ground, and this is her first run in Queensland for the R Drysdale stable. SALUKI (10) has the stronger exposed sprint form, having led and fought on for fourth in a Eagle Farm Mdn, beaten a length and a half, after a sound Toowoomba third. The 1.5kg claim helps and she should be right in this. IT'SALL ABOUT MARY (5) comes off the clearest near-miss, beaten a nose at Kilcoy in a Mdn, and her consistency this season makes her a major player if she handles the first look at 800m. STORM PETAL (7) resumes from a two-month freshening for Kris Zahmel, was only beaten four and a half lengths at Doomben, and has already placed at around this distance, which keeps her firmly in the mix. MISHANI OSCAR (3) resuming today but will be fitter for a recent trial. Place.",
